10/1 - Set up pfSense VM. 

- Downloaded .iso from Internet Archive to avoid installer on pfSense’s website.
- Name: pfSense-HomeSOC Lab Router
- type: BSD
- version: FreeBSD (64-bit)
- 1GB RAM
- 1 vCPU
- Disk: 8GB
- Network Adapters:
    - Adapter 1 (WAN): Attached to NAT — this is pfSense's internet-facing side
    - Adapter 2 (LAN): Attached to Internal Network
        - Network name: soclabnet
    - Both use the Intel PRO/1000 MT Desktop adapter type

pfSense set up well, I needed to redo my virtual hard disk because it didn’t allocate correctly (It only had 1 GB of storage and pfSense said it didn’t recognize any drive). Once I redid it, pfSense set up smoothly with em0 = WAN and em1 = LAN
